msgid "Here is the full program's output:"
msgstr "Hier die Ausgabe des vollständigen Programms:"

#: ../../howto/a-conceptual-overview-of-asyncio.rst:593
msgid ""
"$ python custom-async-sleep.py\n"
"Beginning asynchronous sleep at time: 14:52:22.\n"
"I like work. Work work.\n"
"I like work. Work work.\n"
"I like work. Work work.\n"
"Done asynchronous sleep at time: 14:52:25."
msgstr ""
"$ python custom-async-sleep.py\n"
"Beginning asynchronous sleep at time: 14:52:22.\n"
"I like work. Work work.\n"
"I like work. Work work.\n"
"I like work. Work work.\n"
"Done asynchronous sleep at time: 14:52:25."

#: ../../howto/a-conceptual-overview-of-asyncio.rst:602
msgid ""
"You might feel this implementation of asynchronous sleep was unnecessarily "
"convoluted. And, well, it was. The example was meant to showcase the "
"versatility of futures with a simple example that could be mimicked for more "
"complex needs. For reference, you could implement it without futures, like "
"so::"
msgstr ""
"Du findest diese Umsetzung des asynchronen Schlafens vielleicht unnötig "
"verwickelt. Und das war sie auch. Das Beispiel sollte die Vielseitigkeit von "
"Futures an einem einfachen Fall zeigen, der sich für komplexere Bedürfnisse "
"nachbauen lässt. Zum Vergleich: Du könntest es auch ohne Futures umsetzen, "
"etwa so::"

#: ../../howto/a-conceptual-overview-of-asyncio.rst:609
msgid ""
"async def simpler_async_sleep(seconds):\n"
"    time_to_wake = time.time() + seconds\n"
"    while True:\n"
"        if time.time() >= time_to_wake:\n"
"            return\n"
"        else:\n"
"            await YieldToEventLoop()"
msgstr ""
"async def simpler_async_sleep(seconds):\n"
"    time_to_wake = time.time() + seconds\n"
"    while True:\n"
"        if time.time() >= time_to_wake:\n"
"            return\n"
"        else:\n"
"            await YieldToEventLoop()"

